# core-harness · slim always-on rule core (the ≤10k SessionStart-injected set).
# One rule filename per line, relative to core-harness/rules/. '#' comments + blank lines ignored.
# session-start-rules.sh cat's each listed file, concatenates, caps at 9500 chars (headroom under
# the 10,000-char additionalContext cap), and injects it on SessionStart for PLUGIN adopters (who
# have NO native always-on-rules channel). The FULL 21-rule corpus loads natively via
# /harness:bootstrap → .claude/rules/ (symlink/copy), so this slim set is the gap-filler.
#
# CURATION (W7, 2026-06-09): the 3 hard always-on CONSTRAINTS that must fire on EVERY action
# regardless of which skill is invoked, sized to fit the cap WITHOUT mid-rule truncation
# (3715 + 2731 + 1821 = 8267 chars). Priority order = most-cardinal first.
#   · anti-duplication      — grep-before-write (the explicitly always-on invariant; anti-Frankenstein)
#   · git-safety            — forbidden git ops (no pull/force/--no-verify/add -A)
#   · tdd-mandatory         — tests-first (RED→GREEN→REFACTOR)
# The PROCESS orientation (paradigm 3-planos, story-closure-gate spine, anti-orphan, DoD,
# parallel-safety, …) loads via /harness:bootstrap (full corpus) — it does not fit the slim cap
# and the agent reaches it through the copied .claude/rules/ + the spine skills.
anti-duplication.md
git-safety.md
tdd-mandatory.md
